  "question": {
    "text": "The equilibrium constant for the reaction\n$$\n\\mathrm{SO}_3(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{SO}_2(\\mathrm{~g})+\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{O}_2(\\mathrm{~g})\n$$\nis $\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{c}}=4.9 \\times 10^{-2}$. The value of $\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{c}}$ for the reaction\n$$\n2 \\mathrm{SO}_2(\\mathrm{~g})+\\mathrm{O}_2(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightleftharpoons 2 \\mathrm{SO}_3(\\mathrm{~g})\n$$ \nwill be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n416\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$2.40 \\times 10^{-3}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$9.8 \\times 10^{-2}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$4.9 \\times 10^{-2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{c}}^{\\prime} & =\\left(\\frac{1}{4.9 \\times 10^{-2}}\\right)^2 \\\\ & =\\frac{10^4}{4.9 \\times 4.9}=\\frac{100 \\times 100}{24.01} \\\\ & =4.1649 \\times 100 \\\\ & =416.49\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}